{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 2167814,
  "courseSlug": "spring-5-with-spring-boot-2",
  "courseTitle": "Java Spring Framework, Spring Boot, Spring AI - Gen AI",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43034294",
      "title": "Encryption and Decryption",
      "lectureOrder": 319,
      "videoOrder": 318,
      "sourceHash": "ee0bc6da9ce1fed6196f0c9a4e719f714374ede05c06295f6e60978d0ada4e6a",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 3.36,
          "en": "(gentle music)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.36,
          "end": 6,
          "en": "-: In this video, we'll talk about cryptography.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6,
          "end": 7.86,
          "en": "So what happens is, on the internet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.86,
          "end": 10.62,
          "en": "basically you send information between the servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.62,
          "end": 13.83,
          "en": "or from client to server, or server to client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.83,
          "end": 15.12,
          "en": "and when you say you are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.12,
          "end": 17.04,
          "en": "sending this data through the internet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.04,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "anyone in between can check this data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.33,
          "en": "Of course, right, we have something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.33,
          "end": 23.22,
          "en": "called man in middle attack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.22,
          "end": 26.34,
          "en": "Basically, they can see your data, they can modify the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 29.917,
          "en": "So let's say, if person A says to person B,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.917,
          "end": 33.75,
          "en": "\"Hey, let's meet at a cafe at 5:00 PM,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.75,
          "end": 36.577,
          "en": "but then when the data is passing, the person C says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.577,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "\"Okay, I want to make some modification here.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 42.775,
          "en": "So they go there, they change this data from 5:00 to 6:00,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.775,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "and they send it to B.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 48.03,
          "en": "Now, here we are not just doing a passive attack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.03,
          "end": 49.71,
          "en": "where you are able to read the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.71,
          "end": 51.99,
          "en": "you are also doing a active attack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.99,
          "end": 54.12,
          "en": "Now, how do we secure ourself from this attack?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.12,
          "end": 56.637,
          "en": "Now of course there have, we have to use some mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 56.637,
          "end": 59.67,
          "en": "where at least other person cannot see your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.67,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "Even if they can see data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 63.06,
          "en": "they should not be able to read it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 63.06,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "And second, they should not be able to make the changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 66.72,
          "en": "Even if they make the changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 66.72,
          "end": 70.38,
          "en": "B should be able to know that something has changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.38,
          "end": 73.05,
          "en": "and we can do that with the help of cryptography.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 73.05,
          "end": 74.4,
          "en": "Now, in cryptography we use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 74.4,
          "end": 76.77,
          "en": "a concept of encryption and decryption.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "So let's say when A, is sending data to B now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 82.08,
          "en": "what you can do is you can do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.08,
          "end": 83.91,
          "en": "called an encryption here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 83.91,
          "end": 85.38,
          "en": "Now, to do the encryption,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 85.38,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "what we basically do is we use a key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "and we change our data in such a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 93.27799999999999,
          "en": "that no one else can read it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 93.27799999999999,
          "end": 95.72999999999999,
          "en": "Of course, when you send the same data to B,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 97.95,
          "en": "B cannot read that data now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 97.95,
          "end": 100.74000000000001,
          "en": "That's weird, I mean, we wanted B to know the data, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 100.74000000000001,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "But then, what if you can share the key with B?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 106.08,
          "en": "And now B should be able to decrypt it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 106.08,
          "end": 108.09,
          "en": "So, encryption simply means converting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 108.09,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "your normal text to cipher text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 112.8,
          "en": "And decryption simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 112.8,
          "end": 115.59,
          "en": "that you're converting your cipher text to a normal text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 115.59,
          "end": 119.00999999999999,
          "en": "So when A is writing the content, that will be your,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 119.00999999999999,
          "end": 120.57,
          "en": "and that's your normal text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 120.57,
          "end": 123.21,
          "en": "but then you have to encrypt it so that no one can read it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 123.21,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "Even A cannot read that now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 127.986,
          "en": "Of course, A can read if A can decrypt it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 127.986,
          "end": 131.52,
          "en": "but now when you send this data to B, now B cannot read it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "so they have to decrypt it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 134.7,
          "en": "and they will simply, they can be able to read that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 134.7,
          "end": 137.1,
          "en": "Now, even if C is able to get the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 137.1,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "C cannot read that because it is encrypted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 141.66,
          "en": "Now, how can B read it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 141.66,
          "end": 145.8,
          "en": "Because B has a key, C has no idea what that key is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 145.8,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "Now, this key is important here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 149.37,
          "en": "Now, this key can be of two different types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 149.37,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "A key can be a symmetric key or it can be a asymmetric key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 155.76,
          "en": "So in the symmetric key, what you have is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 155.76,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "you have keys which are same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 160.077,
          "en": "So A and B will have the same keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 160.077,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "And of course, this can be any normal text or normal string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 166.35,
          "en": "which you can use as a key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 167.76,
          "en": "but they will be having the same key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 167.76,
          "end": 171.36,
          "en": "So if A is encrypting the data with this key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 171.36,
          "end": 174.333,
          "en": "the same key has to be there with B as well to decrypt it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 174.333,
          "end": 177.39,
          "en": "This is called a symmetric cryptography,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 177.39,
          "end": 179.35,
          "en": "or symmetric key cryptography.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 179.35,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "The problem with this is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 184.95,
          "en": "this key need to be shared before the communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 187.14,
          "en": "Of course, they cannot share this key on the internet now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 187.14,
          "end": 189.78,
          "en": "because if they share this key on the internet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 189.78,
          "end": 192.277,
          "en": "C can see the key and then C will say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 192.277,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "\"Okay, I got the key, now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "Even if you encrypted, I can read that.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 197.07,
          "en": "So that's one challenge here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 199.32,
          "en": "This key need to be shared beforehand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 199.32,
          "end": 202.23,
          "en": "Maybe they can meet somewhere in person,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 202.23,
          "end": 205.17000000000002,
          "en": "share the key and go back and do the communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 205.17000000000002,
          "end": 207.32999999999998,
          "en": "Again, a weird way of sharing a key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 207.32999999999998,
          "end": 209.55,
          "en": "but again, it's very famous,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 209.55,
          "end": 211.89,
          "en": "the symmetric cryptography, it is faster,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 211.89,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "and you can also have a large key size,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 216.84,
          "en": "and the bigger the key size you have, it's more secure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 216.84,
          "end": 219.72,
          "en": "The challenge is of course the key sharing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 219.72,
          "end": 222.36,
          "en": "And also, what if you have multiple members in the network?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 222.36,
          "end": 223.74,
          "en": "We have D, E,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 223.74,
          "end": 226.29,
          "en": "and maybe A want to do communications with D now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 226.29,
          "end": 227.94,
          "en": "So of course, they have to use a different key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 227.94,
          "end": 230.61,
          "en": "They cannot use the same key which is shared by A and B.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 230.61,
          "end": 235.56,
          "en": "Maybe if you say K1 is the key used by A and B,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 235.56,
          "end": 237.84,
          "en": "now A cannot use the same key with D,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 237.84,
          "end": 240.39,
          "en": "they need to have a different key, let's say K2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 240.39,
          "end": 242.73,
          "en": "What if D wants to communicate with E?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 242.73,
          "end": 245.55,
          "en": "Of course, they have to have a different key, which is K3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 245.55,
          "end": 248.46,
          "en": "That's how you basically have multiple keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 248.46,
          "end": 250.23,
          "en": "in symmetric key cryptography.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 250.23,
          "end": 253.08,
          "en": "And the problem is, managing this key becomes difficult.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 253.08,
          "end": 255.21,
          "en": "What if A want to communicate with everyone?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 255.21,
          "end": 257.28,
          "en": "So A has to manage those number of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 257.28,
          "end": 258.87,
          "en": "those amount of keys with A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 261.31,
          "en": "The solution for this is asymmetric cryptography,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 261.31,
          "end": 263.16,
          "en": "where you don't have a symmetric key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 263.16,
          "end": 265.02,
          "en": "Of course, that's what asymmetric means.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 265.02,
          "end": 266.76,
          "en": "But what you basically have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 266.76,
          "end": 269.28,
          "en": "is you have a concept of public and private key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 269.28,
          "end": 270.21,
          "en": "Now, how this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 270.21,
          "end": 273.023,
          "en": "For the encryption and decryption, you'll be using two keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 273.023,
          "end": 275.49,
          "en": "encrypt the public key and a private key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 275.49,
          "end": 276.84000000000003,
          "en": "And how that works is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 276.84000000000003,
          "end": 280.05,
          "en": "if you encrypt a data with a private key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 280.05,
          "end": 282.75,
          "en": "then you have to decrypt the data with a public key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 282.75,
          "end": 284.85,
          "en": "And when you encrypt the data with public key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 284.85,
          "end": 286.47,
          "en": "you have to decrypt the data with private key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 286.47,
          "end": 287.947,
          "en": "So basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 287.947,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "you have to use the opposite keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 290.94,
          "en": "for encryption, decryption.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 290.94,
          "end": 293.31,
          "en": "You can't use same key for both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 293.31,
          "end": 294.54,
          "en": "Now, what happens is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 294.54,
          "end": 296.19,
          "en": "now since private key is a private key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 296.19,
          "end": 298.83,
          "en": "only the owner knows the private key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 298.83,
          "end": 299.82,
          "en": "What about the public key?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "Public key is known by everyone in the network. Okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 304.8,
          "en": "Now, what's the advantage of this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 304.8,
          "end": 305.76,
          "en": "So, let's say there's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 305.76,
          "end": 308.37,
          "en": "a public key and private key with the B,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 308.37,
          "end": 310.23,
          "en": "and now A wants to send data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 310.23,
          "end": 312.873,
          "en": "Now, a question arise, what key A will use.",
